-c4f4-5a08-ac86-9b0bab51ed69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376678} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa64aea-91f1-5db6-a7b5-4b2bb0f358c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)+{t}_{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50f83e43-d0b2-506c-b5ff-a5ea4f8e05b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376677} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1b80a59-df9c-5a1f-81cb-080366d8b916" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5322e2fa-cf73-52ff-9285-10fe1b776fba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376681} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ca9c69-50b3-51a3-93fa-405eb17a7043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)+{t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376682} {:answer/id #uuid "48702f4e-422c-548d-baf1-022f5967c68a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376683} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e22b40-32f9-5822-bbdd-cdc52bf07bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8e22b40-32f9-5822-bbdd-cdc52bf07bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376684} :answer-field/id #uuid "55684c8c-bbd2-5dd9-a355-2a2b80ebe4b7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186376680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a3cf9875-3059-51ba-adcf-e3e9f02e0ac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-335425" :question/problem "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line\n{{field-2}}\nby substituting \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L9}$ follows from line $\\text{L7}$ by  \n{{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Differentiating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ and applying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating and using the product rule}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$, $\\text{L5}$, and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L4}$ we have\n\n$$\ny(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nUsing $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ from $\\text{L5}$, this becomes\n\n$$\ny(t)-x({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nso\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substituting $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$, $\\text{L8}$, and $\\text{L9}.$ From $\\text{L8}$ we know that\n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$ into\n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L9}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by $\\text{substituting }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t).$"}]}
